2026-10-26T09:11:46.9952463Z [36;1m# Note: There is currently no way to distinguish between undefined variables and empty strings in GitHub Actions.[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9953305Z [36;1m# This limitation affects how we handle default values and empty inputs.[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9954113Z [36;1m# For more information, see: https://github.com/actions/runner/issues/924[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9954680Z [36;1m[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9955164Z [36;1m# The following logic implements the configuration priority described in the README:[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9955715Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9955986Z [36;1m# Inputs[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9956281Z [36;1m# Environment Variables[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9956612Z [36;1m# Config File[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9956902Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9957160Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9957692Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9958580Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9959418Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9960260Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9960961Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9961607Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided() {[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9961952Z [36;1m  local var_name="$1"[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9962280Z [36;1m  local input_value="$2"[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9962639Z [36;1m  local default_value="$3"[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9962961Z [36;1m[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9963334Z [36;1m  if [ -n "$input_value" ] && [ "$input_value" != "$default_value" ]; then[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9963953Z [36;1m    # If action was provided with explicit input by the caller set that[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9964629Z [36;1m    # Use printf %q to safely escape special characters and prevent command injection[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9965279Z [36;1m    printf 'export %s=%q\n' "$var_name" "$input_value" >> trivy_envs.txt[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9965734Z [36;1m  fi[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9965996Z [36;1m}[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9966235Z [36;1m[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9966608Z [36;1m# Set environment variables, handling those with default values[0m
2026-10-26T09:11:46.9967366Z [36;1m# cf. https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/#environment-variables[0m
